# act (nektos/act) runner-label → image mappings for this repo.
#
# Our CI jobs run on a self-hosted runner declared as
# `runs-on: [self-hosted, Linux, X64]` inside the shared CI container
# `ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest`. act needs each of those labels
# mapped to a local image so it schedules the job against the same container CI
# uses — making a local `act` run execute the *unmodified* workflow YAML in the
# same environment as CI. See evals/README.md ("Running an eval locally").
#
# Only repo-wide-correct defaults belong here. Run-specific flags
# (--pull=false, --artifact-server-path) stay on the command line.
#
# Node-injection note (act gap, NOT an image defect): GitHub's runner agent
# mounts `node` into a `container:` job at runtime (externals at /__e); stock
# act does not, and `--container-options` is discarded for a YAML-pinned
# `container:` (RunContext.options(), run_context.go:783). ci-runner correctly
# omits `node`, so bare `act` stops at the first JS action with
# `exec: "node": not found`. To run a container-job workflow end to end, use
# evals/scripts/run-local-act.sh (downloads a glibc node20 and injects it into
# the job container at startup) — image unchanged, local `:latest` untouched.
# Full mechanism + the three working approaches: docs/testing.md ("Running CI
# workflows locally with act"). Upstream gap: nektos/act#107.
# Do NOT add node to the ci-runner image (shared by ~16 workflows); do NOT
# overwrite the local `:latest` tag (the self-hosted runner uses it).
-P self-hosted=ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest
-P Linux=ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest
-P X64=ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest
